### Describe the bug

When parallel tools are used, the tool response Crush generates cause a failure response from LLM.

`Please ensure that the number of function response parts is equal to the number of function call parts of the function call turn.`

The issue appears that certain providers of Gemini models appear to have a stricter schema than others and if the LLM sends a single ModelRole with 6 tools then it expects the the response to also be a single ModelRole with 6 responses but 6 ModelRole's with 1 response each are sent back instead.

### Setup

 - Crush with Gemini provider

### To Reproduce

Steps to reproduce the behavior:
1. Setup Gemini provider; most likely specific to Vertex AI as the provider
2. Initialize Project so that 6 parallel glob tools are issued in a single Model Role from Gemini.

### Source Code

Gemini pointed out the issue when I provided it the complete tool response message and generated this code which solves the problem for me but could use review by people more familiar with this code.  I did test on both AI Studio as provider (which current Crush works with without patch) as well as Vertex AI provider and works fine with both.

```
diff --git a/internal/llm/provider/gemini.go b/internal/llm/provider/gemini.go
index 21f4e65d..e5aa9b2b 100644
--- a/internal/llm/provider/gemini.go
+++ b/internal/llm/provider/gemini.go
@@ -99,6 +99,7 @@ func (g *geminiClient) convertMessages(messages []message.Message) []*genai.Cont
 			}

 		case message.Tool:
+			var toolParts []*genai.Part
 			for _, result := range msg.ToolResults() {
 				response := map[string]any{"result": result.Content}
 				parsed, err := parseJSONToMap(result.Content)
@@ -118,16 +119,17 @@ func (g *geminiClient) convertMessages(messages []message.Message) []*genai.Cont
 					}
 				}

-				history = append(history, &genai.Content{
-					Parts: []*genai.Part{
-						{
-							FunctionResponse: &genai.FunctionResponse{
-								Name:     toolCall.Name,
-								Response: response,
-							},
-						},
+				toolParts = append(toolParts, &genai.Part{
+					FunctionResponse: &genai.FunctionResponse{
+						Name:     toolCall.Name,
+						Response: response,
 					},
-					Role: genai.RoleModel,
+				})
+			}
+			if len(toolParts) > 0 {
+				history = append(history, &genai.Content{
+					Parts: toolParts,
+					Role:  genai.RoleModel,
 				})
 			}
 		}
```

